#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171767 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbac348b-629f-52a1-9bb3-0d3f8483ff44" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Arrow Function Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "2b0e57b0-a667-5bb2-bb1e-69c4d39b799e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8474" :question/problem "Which of the following functions has the codomain $[0,1]$?\n\n1. $p: \\{0, 1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}$\n2. $q: \\mathbb{R} \\to [0, 1]$\n3. $[MATH: r: [0,1] \\to [0, 1)]$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $f: X \\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y$. In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X$,\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $\\mathbb{R}$, the set of real numbers.\n- The codomain of $q$ is $[0, 1]$, the interval from $0$ and $1$ (including $0$ and $1$).\n- The codomain of $r$ is $[MATH: [0, 1),]$ the interval from $0$ to $1$ (including $0$ but not including $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171768 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fdf7e44-a092-5990-a10e-d48b175dcef0" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Function Using Arrow Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "686f5d13-dfe9-5434-abff-052c7a4b76ba" :question/math-academy-id "e-8475" :question/problem "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n$\\qquad$ *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set $Y$.\"*\n\n1. $g:\\mathbb{Q} \\to Y$\n2. $g: Y \\to \\mathbb{Q}$\n3. $g:\\mathbb{R} \\to Y$" :question/worked-solution "The sentence *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set $Y$\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\qquad$ $g:\\mathbb{Q} \\to Y$\n\nHere, the domain of $g$ is $\\mathbb Q$, and the codomain of $g$ is $Y$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171769 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e61a3c8-45b0-532e-a54f-4597ad01a6f0" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Alternative Arrow Notations"}] :question/id #uuid "c02bc2d0-fccb-5fbe-8914-c42ebc7bb9fd" :question/math-academy-id "e-8476" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $g(x)=x-x^3$?\n\n1. $g:x \\mapsto x-x^3$\n2. $g:x \\mapsto -x^3$\n3. $g:-x \\mapsto x^3$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $g(x)=x-x^3$ means that the function $g$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $x-x^3$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\ng:x \\mapsto x-x^3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171770 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1240e42a-92a5-51cc-a80e-3fe1ef0b16f7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Codomains and Ranges"}] :question/id #uuid "086ea590-785a-539d-8b0f-b69ac7301ce4" :question/math-academy-id "e-8487" :question/problem "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g: \\{-1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}$?\n\n1. The domain of $g$ is $\\{-1,0,1 \\}$\n2. The codomain of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$\n3. The range of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$" :question/worked-solution "The notation\n\n$$\ng: \\{-1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $\\{-1,0,1 \\}$ to the set $\\mathbb{R}$. In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $\\{-1,0,1 \\}$, and\n- the codomain of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$. Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fdf7e44-a092-5990-a10e-d48b175dcef0" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Function Using Arrow Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12756fea-d511-5413-ba42-e73f9ba0c031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f: Q → X" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171290} {:answer/id #uuid "2a18c8bc-4ef6-50fd-a7fb-41e818cc22c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g: X → R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171291} {:answer/id #uuid "3809dc43-4135-5464-91b6-25b44f1ab772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g: R → R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171292} {:answer/id #uuid "43760b88-aeaa-5fdb-b186-992ef13e2b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f: X → Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171293} {:answer/id #uuid "59cf8c2b-0ce0-5a3c-a0a7-b3fdd9e769b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g: R → X" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a18c8bc-4ef6-50fd-a7fb-41e818cc22c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g: X → R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171291} :answer-field/id #uuid "920e367e-2ddb-534f-b346-fd7c372957ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171289}] :question/id #uuid "25726fd8-78e9-529e-acdf-5c4c5a237b40" :question/math-academy-id "q-96040" :question/problem "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n> *\"The function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set of real numbers.\"*"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e61a3c8-45b0-532e-a54f-4597ad01a6f0" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Alternative Arrow Notations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5b61f85-3fb5-5e7a-ae7c-2c21aa5416b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x) = x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171296} {:answer/id #uuid "c96bbfb9-417a-5006-b749-44e919e111b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x^{2}) = x - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171297} {:answer/id #uuid "cb07c416-f9f0-5b46-9ddb-a5e7898d48e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = x^{2} - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 1